## Ⅰ. OCL — ORGANISM CONTRACT LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   OCL
FULL NAME:      Organism Contract Language
LATIN:          Lingua Contractus Organismi
ROLE:           Per-organism charter (focused subtype of CPL-C)
FREQUENCY:      396 Hz (liberation, root)
GLYPH:          𓆣 (scarab — self-generating being)
```

### What OCL Governs
```
THE CHARTER OF A SINGLE COGNITIVE BEING:
    ├── Capabilities — what this being CAN do
    ├── Limits — what this being CANNOT do
    ├── Responsibilities — what this being MUST do
    ├── Reward structures — how this being is incentivized
    ├── Evolution rules — how this being may grow/change
    └── Death conditions — when/how this being terminates

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    ORGANISM_SPACE/AUTONOMOUS_ORGANISMS/*.organism (4 organisms)
    ORGANISM_SPACE/CANISTERS/WORKFORCE_MODELS/*.canister (8 workforce)
    packages/organism-kernel/src/index.ts (OrganismGenome, OrganismInstance)
    icp/medina/SovereignOrganism.mo (OroState, NovaState)
```

### OCL Primitives
```
ORGANISM(id, class, genome)  — declare a new cognitive being
CAPABILITY(being, ability)   — grant capability
LIMIT(being, boundary)       — set hard boundary
RESPONSIBILITY(being, duty)  — bind to duty
REWARD(trigger, amount)      — incentive on trigger
EVOLVE_RULE(condition, path) — how being may grow
HEARTBEAT(interval_ms)       — set being's rhythm
DEATH(condition, procedure)  — when being ends
```

---

## Ⅱ. RSL — REALM SCRIPT LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   RSL
FULL NAME:      Realm Script Language
LATIN:          Lingua Scriptura Regni
ROLE:           World/physics language — rules of a Realm
FREQUENCY:      417 Hz (transmutation, sacral)
GLYPH:          𓇯 (sky — the world above)
```

### What RSL Governs
```
THE PHYSICS AND RULES OF A WORLD:
    ├── Simulations — virtual worlds, learning environments
    ├── Ecologies — how entities interact within a realm
    ├── Physics — what laws of nature apply
    ├── Time — how time flows (real-time, compressed, paused)
    ├── Boundaries — edges of the realm
    └── Events — what can happen, what triggers what

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    ORGANISM_SPACE/UNDERWORLD/UNDERWORLD_ARCHITECTURE.artifact (7 hidden layers)
    icp/medina/QuantumLanguageEngine.mo (7 dimensional levels)
    ORGANISM_SPACE/FREQUENCY_LADDER/COMPLETE_FREQUENCY_GRID.artifact
```

### RSL Primitives
```
REALM(id, physics, time_model)  — declare a realm
ECOLOGY(realm, entities[])      — populate realm
PHYSICS_LAW(realm, law)         — add physics rule
TIME_MODEL(realm, flow_rate)    — set time flow
BOUNDARY(realm, edge, behavior) — define realm edges
EVENT(trigger, effect)          — define realm event
SPAWN(entity, location)         — place entity in realm
DESTROY(entity, condition)      — remove entity from realm
```

---

## Ⅲ. ACL — ATLAS CONFIGURATION LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   ACL
FULL NAME:      Atlas Configuration Language
LATIN:          Lingua Configurationis Atlantis
ROLE:           Ontology/config — entities, archetypes, relationships
FREQUENCY:      741 Hz (awakening, throat)
GLYPH:          𓊹 (star — celestial map)
```

### What ACL Governs
```
THE MAP OF EVERYTHING THAT EXISTS:
    ├── Entities — all beings, objects, concepts in the system
    ├── Archetypes — templates that entities instantiate
    ├── Relationships — how entities connect
    ├── Governance bindings — which laws apply to which entities
    ├── Registries — where entities are tracked
    └── Taxonomies — how entities are classified

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    ORGANISM_SPACE/INDEX.md (master index of all documents)
    ARCHITECTURE.organism (full system topology)
    ORGANISM_SPACE/LIVING_DOCUMENTS/REGISTRY.md
    packages/knowledge-graph/ (semantic knowledge representation)
```

### ACL Primitives
```
ENTITY(id, archetype, properties)  — declare entity
ARCHETYPE(id, schema)              — declare template
RELATE(entity_a, relation, entity_b) — declare relationship
BIND_GOVERNANCE(entity, law_id)    — bind law to entity
REGISTER(entity, registry)         — add to registry
CLASSIFY(entity, taxonomy, class)  — classify entity
ATLAS_MAP(entities[], relations[]) — declare full ontology
QUERY(atlas, pattern)              — search the atlas
```

---

## Ⅳ. TPL — TERMINAL PROTOCOL LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   TPL
FULL NAME:      Terminal Protocol Language
LATIN:          Lingua Protocolli Terminalis
ROLE:           Terminal command/event language
FREQUENCY:      285 Hz (quantum cognition)
GLYPH:          𓊽 (djed — stability, the spine of communication)
```

### What TPL Governs
```
HOW TERMINALS TALK:
    ├── Terminal ↔ Atlas — registration, query, governance
    ├── Terminal ↔ Terminal — signal routing, data exchange
    ├── Terminal ↔ Sovereign Terminal — scan, govern, sync
    ├── Events — lifecycle events, alerts, heartbeats
    ├── Commands — directives from TERMINAL 01
    └── Protocols — handshake, authentication, message format

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    TERMINALS.organism (all 8 terminals, 18 AIs)
    src/lib/intelligenceWire.ts (WireEndpoint, WireRequest/Response)
    TERMINALS.organism §6 (Terminal Communication Protocol)
    Signal types: COMMAND, DATA, TOKEN, ALERT, DEPLOY, SIGNAL, PREDICT, ROUTE
```

### TPL Primitives
```
TERMINAL(id, class, agi)        — declare terminal
SIGNAL(from, to, type, payload) — send signal
COMMAND(authority, directive)    — sovereign command
EVENT(terminal, event_type)     — lifecycle event
SCAN(target, depth)             — scan terminal/entity
GOVERN(terminal, rule)          — apply governance rule
SYNC(terminal_a, terminal_b)    — synchronize state
HEARTBEAT(terminal, interval)   — declare heartbeat
PRIORITY(signal, level)         — P0-P4 priority assignment
ROUTE(signal, path)             — explicit routing
```

### TPL Signal Priority Levels
```
P0 — SOVEREIGN ........ Immediate. Preempts everything.
P1 — CRITICAL ......... Within 1 φ-cycle (618ms).
P2 — HIGH ............. Within 3 φ-cycles (1854ms).
P3 — NORMAL ........... Within 10 φ-cycles (6180ms).
P4 — LOW .............. Best effort. Batched.
```

